ts adequately (stress resilience), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but moody, loner (crew cooperation). Good technical and responsibility, but cooperation concerns.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely B has strong reliability and stress, but communication issues may be serious. D has strong technical and responsibility but moody and loner may affect crew. C has good decision and attention but communication and egocentric issues. A has technical and leadership but unfriendly and health.\n\nWhich candidate balances? Maybe D: strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, adequate response to unexpected events. Moodiness and loner could affect crew, but maybe less severe than pretentiousness or egocentric. B's wrong tone could be safety-critical. C's egocentric and communication issues may be worse. A's unfriendly and health issues may affect reliability.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate D, but note concerns. Provide argument.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"to start\". Provide evidence.\n\nLet's produce public message: state recommendation for D, explain strengths and concerns, compare with others.\n\nMetadata vote D."}
